cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Renewing catalyst kinetics: exact and Monte Carlo models of SO2 oxidation on a self renewing copper oxide surface"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22910821
abstract: >-
  Exact master equation and kinetic Monte Carlo models of SO2 oxidation on a
  copper oxide surface that sulphates in service and recovers by exposing fresh
  copper. It contains three results that hold for every positive assignment of
  rate constants. The first is a minimum active patch size of three sites under a
  dual site adsorption mechanism, checked on all 996 connected graphs of up to
  seven sites. The second is a closed form for the share of a randomly deactivated
  lattice that can never turn over, with an exact rate expansion built from small
  components. The third is an exact bound on product recovered per copper atom
  consumed. The reaction barriers are illustrative and the work has not been
  validated against experiment.
keywords:
  - kinetic Monte Carlo
  - master equation
  - heterogeneous catalysis
  - catalyst deactivation
  - sulphation
  - copper oxide
  - site percolation
  - lattice animals
